  data:  # 1419
    kind: invariant  # 1419
    title: "verify-claims: an unparseable function_summaries.d file crashes with exit 1, the 'violated' exit code"  # 1419
    status: violated  # 1419
    priority: 3  # 1419
    parent:  # 1419
    tags:  # 1419
    - catalogue  # 1419
    - verify_claims  # 1419
    isbefore: []  # 1419
    duplicate_of: []  # 1419
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1419
    pr_ref:  # 1419
    description: "Found 2026-10-11 while fixing INV-rirud (PR #1543). Repro (dev e0abdace0a): XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/function_summaries.d/bad.yaml = 'summaries: [unclosed'; 'hypergumbo verify-claims repo --claims claims.yaml' with a taint_flow claim -> exit 1, stderr ends with the YAML parse error and 'This is a bug; re-run with --debug for a full traceback.' Exit 1 is the violated exit code, so a CI gate reads a crash as a violation. The taint arm raises TaintCatalogError (exit 2) for the same input since PR #1542. Under --no-default-overlays the provenance pre-read (taint.split_community_files) would raise TaintCatalogError outside the load's try block, still uncaught. Fix direction: parse failures in the summary loader raise a catalogue error that cmd_verify_claims maps to exit 2, matching the taint arm."  # 1419
    fields:  # 1419
      statement: "A broken catalogue file is a clean exit-2 error naming the file, never an uncaught exception, and never exit 1 (violated)."  # 1419
      root_cause: "load_function_summaries calls yaml.safe_load on every function_summaries.d file with no error handling, and cmd_verify_claims does not catch yaml.YAMLError; the top-level handler exits 1."  # 1419
