- op: discuss  # ff75
  at: '2026-10-12T03:06:46Z'  # ff75
  by: agent  # ff75
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ff75
  clock: 3  # ff75
  nonce: ff75  # ff75
  message: "Fixed in PR #1545 (436a19a122). Root cause: load_function_summaries yaml.safe_loaded with no handling and cmd_verify_claims did not catch it, so main's safety net exited 1; the same class hit the I/O overlay provenance pre-read (overlay_declares_community parsed before the load that would refuse it), silently-skipped wrong-typed overlay sections, frameworks.d (crash), library_signatures.d (py.py reads it at import; registry discovery swallowed the error so the python analyzer vanished, exit 0), dataflow_patterns.d (syntax error skipped), and sketch's cold-cache auto-run (swallowed everything). Fix: one base yaml_catalogs.CatalogueError (TaintCatalogError, IoPrimitiveOverlayError, DuplicateYamlKeyError, DefaultOverlayError derive; summary/framework/library-signature/dataflow loaders raise it), shared read_catalogue_yaml, cli.main maps CatalogueError to 'Error: ...' exit 2; analyzer discovery, analyzer pool and sketch auto-run re-raise it; verify-claims loads summaries in the taint-model try block; summary provenance split uses its own noun. Evidence (dev 436a19a122, filed repro): function_summaries.d/bad.yaml='summaries: [unclosed', 'hypergumbo verify-claims repo --claims claims.yaml --input hg.json' with a taint_flow claim -> rc=2, 'Error: could not parse function summary file $T/xdg/hypergumbo/function_summaries.d/bad.yaml: while parsing a flow sequence' (before: rc=1 'This is a bug'). Live harness: 15 verify-claims channels x {syntax, shape, field} with and without --no-default-overlays all rc=2 naming the file; survey and sketch x frameworks.d/library_signatures.d/dataflow_patterns.d x 3 all rc=2. Filed INV-horob for the results-cache key ignoring user analysis-stage channels."  # ff75
